// lib/i18n/translations.js
//
// Translation dictionary for OmniFin Portal's UI text — nav labels,
// the core trading vocabulary (Buy/Sell, Profit/Loss), and the
// homepage's visible content (Hero, the 3 ecosystem sections, the
// Supported Currencies section). Consumed by
// lib/i18n/LanguageContext.js's useLanguage()/t() and, for the
// zero-imports app/calculators/page.jsx, by an identical inline copy
// of just the 4 trading-term keys that page needs (see that file's
// own comment).
//
// SCOPE NOTE: this covers the header nav and the homepage — the
// site's main entry point and most-translated-expected surface — plus
// the calculator's core trading terms. It is not yet a full
// line-by-line translation of every sentence on every inner page
// (Academy lessons, News, Community, etc.); that remains a larger,
// ongoing effort. Every language here covers the same key set, so
// adding a new translatable string anywhere in the app just means
// adding one more key to each language's object below (missing keys
// fall back to English via translate()'s lookup, so a
// partially-translated addition never renders blank).
//
// INTERPOLATION: a value may contain "{paramName}" placeholders (e.g.
// "{currencyCount}+ world currencies"). translate(lang, key, params)
// replaces each placeholder with params[paramName] when provided.
//
// Roman Urdu ("ur-Latn") is listed first after English, per the
// product requirement that it be a prominent option — most Pakistani
// users read and type Urdu in Latin script in everyday apps far more
// than the Nasta'liq script, so this isn't just "Urdu without the
// script," it's the dominant real-world register.

